"Lab asgard-odin-ai  (domain lab.geeko.me, TLS letsencrypt)

Harvesters
  asgard  https://asgard.lab.example.com  (TLS not verified)
    networks: untagged, vlan20 (dhcp) (lb 10.29.20.200-10.29.20.220) [default]
    storage class: longhorn-single (1 replica)
    images: leap-16 (download)

Hosts
  odin  VM on asgard, leap-16, 4 CPU / 8Gi / 40Gi, network vlan20
    odin.lab.geeko.me  profiles: rke2 → cert-manager → harvester-cloud-provider → outrider → sprouter → rancher → ai-factory → ai-demos
  dgx-spark  existing machine jeroen@dgx-spark.lab.geeko.me, leap-16
    dgx-spark.lab.geeko.me  profiles: none

Downstream clusters
  heimdall  k3s on asgard, managed by Rancher on odin, labels needs-traefik=true, needs-storage=true, needs-observability=true, annotations hosted-domain=lab.geeko.me
    pool all: 1 × 12 CPU / 40Gi / 500Gi, leap-16, network vlan20 [etcd, controlplane, worker]
    Fleet profiles: traefik, storage, observability (installed by Fleet)
  freya  rke2 on asgard, managed by Rancher on odin, labels needs-storage=true, needs-sbomscanner=true, needs-cnpg=true, annotations hosted-domain=lab.geeko.me
    pool all: 1 × 4 CPU / 16Gi / 100Gi, leap-16, network vlan20 [etcd, controlplane, worker]
    Fleet profiles: storage, sbomscanner, cloudnative-pg (installed by Fleet)
    profiles: opentelemetry → open-webui → suse-observability-agent (ChartProfiles, installed by the engine)
  dgx  metal rke2, managed by Rancher on odin, labels has-gpu=nvidia, annotations hosted-domain=lab.geeko.me
    node dgx-spark [etcd, controlplane, worker]
    Fleet profiles: gpu-operator (installed by Fleet)
    profiles: suse-observability-agent → vllm → opentelemetry (ChartProfiles, installed by the engine)

Fleet (Rancher on odin)
  groups: all-downstream-clusters
  repo ai-apps  https://github.com/SUSE-Technical-Marketing/suse-rancher-prime-setup.git@main /apps/ai
  repo lab-setup-appco  https://github.com/SUSE-Technical-Marketing/suse-rancher-prime-setup.git@main /apps/appco → all-downstream-clusters
  repo lab-setup-base  https://github.com/SUSE-Technical-Marketing/suse-rancher-prime-setup.git@main /apps/base → all-downstream-clusters
  repo lab-setup-demos  https://github.com/SUSE-Technical-Marketing/suse-rancher-prime-setup.git@main /apps/demos
  repo fleet-local/lab-setup-local  https://github.com/SUSE-Technical-Marketing/suse-rancher-prime-setup.git@main /apps/local
  repo lab-setup-platform  https://github.com/SUSE-Technical-Marketing/suse-rancher-prime-setup.git@main /apps/platform
  repo lab-setup-suse  https://github.com/SUSE-Technical-Marketing/suse-rancher-prime-setup.git@main /apps/suse
  repo lab-setup-thirdparty  https://github.com/SUSE-Technical-Marketing/suse-rancher-prime-setup.git@main /apps/thirdparty
  helmop suse-observability  suse-observability 2.12.0 from https://charts.rancher.com/server-charts/prime/suse-observability → needs-observability=true

Kubernetes secrets and configmaps
  secret fleet-default/application-collection-basicauth on odin  username, password
  secret fleet-default/fleet-secrets on odin  appco-values.yaml, harbor-values.yaml, suse-registry-values.yaml, cert-manager-values.yaml, suse-observability-values.yaml
  secret fleet-default/scc-suse-basicauth on odin  username, password

Secrets
  ok       appco (username + password)
  ok       cloudflare (token)
  ok       nvidia (username + password)
  ok       observability (license + password + token)
  ok       rancher-admin
  ok       routeros (username + password)
  ok       scc (username + password)
  ok       ssh-key"
`;

